<title>ROMANIA: Romania Jan-March current account gap $137 mln.</title>
<headline>Romania Jan-March current account gap $137 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's current account posted a $137 million deficit over January-March, down from $493 million in the equivalent period of last year, central bank data (BNR) showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p> ROMANIAN CURRENT A/C	 JAN-MARCH 97	 JAN-MARCH 96</p>
<p> Current account (million USD)	-137		    -493</p>
<p> Trade balance			-184		    -403</p>
<p> Exports (FOB)		     1,924		   1,946</p>
<p> Imports (FOB)		     2,108		   2,349</p>
<p> Services balance		    +31		     -82</p>
<p> Income balance			-70		     -91</p>
<p> Current transfers balance	 +86		     +83</p>
<p>NOTE: Romania's government aims to slash the current account deficit to $1.4 billion this year from an estimated $2.3 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
